  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Bill of Rights guaranteeing housing, education, healthcare, decent work and a minimum wage; rebuild the NHS and expand public health; raise Child Benefit, restore benefits for 16–17s, increase state pensions, end means-testing for residential care; free nursery education for all 3–4-year-olds and 700 extra teachers; tackle the housing crisis with new homes, renovations, and energy efficiency; fair personal taxation with a 15p starter rate and wider basic band; adopt the EU Social Chapter and a Charter for Trade Union rights; redirect spending from nuclear weapons to public services. TEXT_G: Secure a national debate and a fair referendum on Europe; ask whether to join a federal Europe or return to an association of sovereign nations; emphasize the urgency of safeguarding sovereignty; criticize other parties for offering only a single-currency referendum.",
